-- title:
--   Edge-chart unit locus as a finite union of linear pieces
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic base.** Let $r$ be a prime and let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero integral domain, assumed by `hdvr` to be a discrete valuation ring, with $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible (`h\pi`), $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`, absolute unramifiedness). Let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficients.** Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero integral domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every $x \in Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^r \pmod \pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** Let $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a group homomorphism such that, by `hvdet`, $v\!\det(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Group data.** Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma \le G$ a subgroup, such that some $z \in \Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix with $v\!\det(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and some $w \in \Gamma$ has $v\!\det(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`); let $\Gamma' \le G$ be characterised by `h\Gamma'` as the set of elements of $\Gamma$ with even $v\!\det \circ \sigma$. Let $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be the homomorphism sending $g$ to the class of $\sigma g$ (`h\rho`). The hypotheses `hdisc` and `hcocpt` require the action of the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ on the vertices of the lattice tree $\mathrm{Vertex}\,\mathcal O\,K_0$ (homothety classes of full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$) to have finite vertex stabilisers inside $\rho(\Gamma')$ and finitely many orbits, the latter in the form: there is a finite set $S$ of vertices meeting every orbit.
--
--   **Model and moduli identification.** Let $\mathcal X$ be a scheme with a proper flat morphism $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O$. For an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, write $\widehat\Omega^{\mathrm{nr}}(B) = (Onr \to_{\mathcal O\text{-alg}} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(\pi, B)$ for the value at $B$ of `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)`, a Deligne datum over $B$ being an assignment $M \mapsto \mathrm{line}(M)$ of a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subseteq K_0^2$ with invertible quotient, monotone under inclusions of lattices, equivariant for scalar matrices, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$; and write $\mathcal X(B)$ for the value at $B$ of `Scheme.nilpPoints f`, the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Let $\Theta$ be a family of maps $\widehat\Omega^{\mathrm{nr}}(B) \to \mathcal X(B)$, one for each such $B$, subject to four hypotheses: `hΘnat`, naturality in $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $B \to B'$; `hΘinv`, invariance under the twisted action of $\Gamma$, namely $\Theta(x') = \Theta(x)$ whenever `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for $\sigma\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma$, i.e. the first component of $x'$ is that of $x$ precomposed with $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$ and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$; `hΘfib`, for every algebraically closed field $k$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi : Onr \to k$, the map $P \mapsto \Theta(\psi, P)$ is onto $\mathcal X(k)$ and two Deligne data have the same image exactly when $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ are related by the twisted action of some $\gamma \in \Gamma$; and `hΘuniv`, the universal property that for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every natural, twisted-$\Gamma$-invariant family $\rho'$ from $\widehat\Omega^{\mathrm{nr}}$ to the nilpotent points of $T$ there is a natural family $u$ from the nilpotent points of $f$ to those of $T$ with $u \circ \Theta = \rho'$, and any natural family with this property agrees with $u$ pointwise.
--
--   **Analytic frame.** Let $C$ be an algebraically closed field which is a $K_0$-algebra, complete and valued with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, and let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $C$ an $R$-algebra, compatibly with the $\mathcal O$- and $K_0$-structures on $C$. Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformizer of $K_0$ in $C$, that is an element $\varpi.\varpi \in K_0$ with $0 < v(\varpi.\varpi) < 1$ in $C$ and such that every nonzero $a \in K_0$ satisfies $v(\varpi.\varpi)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi.\varpi)^{-N}$ for some $N$. The hypothesis `hF` asserts `IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`: $\pi$ is irreducible, $R \to C$ is injective with image exactly the elements of valuation $\le 1$, $R$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the elements of $K_0$ of valuation $\le 1$ are exactly those coming from $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ is closed in $C$, and $\pi$ and $\varpi.\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Let $\psi_0 : Onr \to R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map. Further: `hrk`, for all $x$ with $v(x) < 1$ and all $y \neq 0$ there is $n$ with $v(x)^n \le v(y)$; `hval`, every nonzero $\varepsilon \in \Gamma_0$ dominates $v(y)$ for some $y \neq 0$; `hex`, `Omega.IsExhausted ϖ`, i.e. every $z \in C$ outside the image of $K_0$ lies in one of the affinoids $\mathrm{affinoid}\,\varpi\,n$; and the holomorphic ring `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ ρ` is a domain.
--
--   **Chart data.** Let $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ have matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`), let $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ be arbitrary, and let $t$ be an element of the edge chart ring $A =$ `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r`, the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, Onr)/(\mathtt{edgeRel})$ away from the class `edgeQuot.discr`; this ring carries the two distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η`.
--
--   Finally, let $S \subseteq C$ be a set characterised by `hS` as follows: $z \in S$ if and only if $z$ lies outside the image of $K_0$ in $C$ and, for every adic point $x$ of the formal upper half plane over $R$ (a compatible system $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$ of Deligne data over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$) with coordinate $x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C = z$, and for every $n \in \mathbb N$, there exist a ring homomorphism $\bar x : A/(\pi^{n+1}) \to R/(\pi^{n+1})$ and a Deligne datum $d$ over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$ such that: $\bar x$ composed with the structural map $Onr \to A/(\pi^{n+1})$ is $\psi_0$ reduced modulo $\pi^{n+1}$; $d$ lies in the standard edge chart with coordinates $\bar x(\xi)$ and $\bar x(\eta)$, in the sense that $d.\mathrm{line}$ of the standard full lattice is the span of $\bar x(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, that $d.\mathrm{line}$ of the $g_1$-translate of the standard lattice is the image under `actBaseChange` at $g_1$ of the span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar x(\eta) \otimes e_1$, and that $d$ satisfies `DeligneDatum.InEdgeChart` for the pair (the $g_1$-translate of the standard lattice, the standard lattice), i.e. edge-nondegeneracy at every prime ideal; $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$, that is $(x.\mathrm{pt}\,n).\mathrm{line}\,M$ is the preimage of $d.\mathrm{line}(h^{-1}M)$ under `actBaseChange` at $h^{-1}$ for every full lattice $M$; and the image of $t$ under $\bar x$ is a unit of $R/(\pi^{n+1})$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist $m \in \mathbb N$ and two families of finite sets of pairs $L, M : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathrm{Finset}(C \times C)$ such that:
--
--   (i) for every index $k$, the second coordinate of every pair in $L\,k$ is nonzero;
--
--   (ii) for every index $k$, the second coordinate of every pair in $M\,k$ is nonzero;
--
--   (iii) for every index $k$, the set of those $z \in C$ which lie in the union $\mathrm{vertexTube}\,\varpi\,[h] \cup \mathrm{edgeTube}\,\varpi\,[h] \cup \mathrm{vertexTube}\,\varpi\,[h\cdot\mathrm{edgeFlip}\,K_0\,\varpi]$ (here $[\,\cdot\,]$ denotes the class in $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$, $\mathrm{edgeFlip}\,K_0\,\varpi = \mathrm{diag}(\varpi.\varpi, 1)$, $\mathrm{vertexTube}\,\varpi\,g$ is the set of $z$ outside the image of $K_0$ with $\mathrm{pmoebius}\,g^{-1} z$ in the affinoid of level $0$, and $\mathrm{edgeTube}\,\varpi\,g$ the set of such $z$ with $\mathrm{pmoebius}\,g^{-1}z$ outside the image of $K_0$ and of valuation strictly between $v(\varpi.\varpi)$ and $1$) and which satisfy $v(e_2) \le v(\mathrm{pmoebius}\,[h]^{-1} z - e_1)$ for every pair $(e_1,e_2) \in L\,k$ and $v(\mathrm{pmoebius}\,[h]^{-1} z - e_1) \le v(e_2)$ for every pair $(e_1,e_2) \in M\,k$, is contained in $S$;
--
--   (iv) conversely, every $z \in S$ belongs to one of these $m$ sets, i.e. for some index $k$ it lies in the union of the three tubes above and satisfies the inequalities $v(e_2) \le v(\mathrm{pmoebius}\,[h]^{-1} z - e_1)$ for all $(e_1,e_2) \in L\,k$ and $v(\mathrm{pmoebius}\,[h]^{-1} z - e_1) \le v(e_2)$ for all $(e_1,e_2) \in M\,k$.
--
--   Thus $S$ is exactly the union of $m$ pieces of the closed edge region attached to $h$, each cut out in the coordinate $u = \mathrm{pmoebius}\,[h]^{-1}z$ by finitely many conditions $v(u - e_1) \ge v(e_2)$ and finitely many conditions $v(u - e_1) \le v(e_2)$ with $e_2 \neq 0$.
--
--   In the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation step, this describes the locus where a prescribed element of the standard edge chart ring becomes invertible along a closed edge region of Drinfeld's upper half plane over $C$: it is a finite union of regions defined by valuation inequalities on the translated coordinate $[h]^{-1}z$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient), where such unit loci carry the holomorphic functions obtained by evaluating sections along the uniformisation.
